## 15. Calibration: what a strong accept rests on

Verbatim fit to all six Theme 2 bullets; four new closed-form results, each
with a falsifiable experiment; a memorable central law (`1 - 1/R_0` for
markets of models) that gives talks and reviews a handle; a policy object a
regulator could actually use (the substitution frontier); a complete econ
apparatus of externality, public good and policy triple; and validated
simulator ground truth to anchor it. The honest risks: reviewers who want
fully heterogeneous agents (answered as future work, with the machinery
stated to extend), and the dependence of the clean herd-immunity form on the
strong-correction limit (mitigated by reporting the exact root). Nothing in
the paper claims beyond what is derived or measured at submission time.
